  "ASHRAE Cycle III"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Unit ventilator (terminal unit) controller",
 "applies_to": "Unit ventilators with a chilled water coil and/or a hot water, steam or electric heating coil, run to ASHRAE Cycle III on the Siemens BACnet PTEC unit vent controller 550-493PA.",
 "summary": "Application 6676 controls a unit ventilator to ASHRAE Cycle III on a Siemens BACnet PTEC controller over BACnet MS/TP. Room temperature is held by modulating the coil valves directly (or a face-bypass damper with 2-position valves), and the outdoor air damper holds a mixed air temperature setpoint above its minimum position. It supports 2-pipe or 4-pipe coils, up to three electric heat stages, auxiliary radiation, morning warm-up/cool-down, night override and free cooling.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
  "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
  "Units are given in US units (°F, Btu/lb); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
  "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
  "LOW TEMP DET (BI 26) state texts are printed as Active = OFF and Inactive = ON; they are kept as printed.",
  "With 1 VLV HTGCLG (BO 16) = YES (2-pipe), heat/cool switchover must come from PPCL or the field panel commanding HEAT.COOL; otherwise it is automatic."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "BACnet PTEC Controller Unit Vent - Heating and/or Chilled Water Cooling, ASHRAE Cycle III, Application 6676, Application Note",
  "doc_number": "140-1181",
  "revision_date": "2018-01-23",
  "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/lDFatYOxLHYD043TCJd_1A/content"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing), then release the unit to application control. The BMS commands occupancy with DAY.NGT (BO 29) and the day setpoints, turns free cooling on and off with FREE CLG (BO 23), and reads room temperature, fan status, outdoor air damper position, the low temperature detector and the error status.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BO 29",
    "name": "DAY.NGT",
    "why": "DAY = occupied, NIGHT = unoccupied"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 23",
    "name": "FREE CLG",
    "why": "Free cooling / economizer enable"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 6",
    "name": "DAY CLG STPT",
    "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 7",
    "name": "DAY HTG STPT",
    "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 5",
    "name": "HEAT.COOL",
    "why": "Current mode: HEAT or COOL"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 50",
    "name": "FAN",
    "why": "Fan on/off"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 4",
    "name": "ROOM TEMP",
    "why": "Space temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 62",
    "name": "OA DMPR POS",
    "why": "Outdoor air damper position, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 26",
    "name": "LOW TEMP DET",
    "why": "Low temperature detection thermostat"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 99",
    "name": "ERROR STATUS",
    "why": "Controller error code"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Occupancy is DAY.NGT (BO 29). With a wall switch on DI 2 and WALL SWITCH (BO 18) = YES, the switch sets it; standalone with no switch the controller stays in day mode; on a network the field panel or BMS commands DAY.NGT. NGT OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary night override from the room unit button.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": "The field panel (or PPCL) turns the free cooling/economizer function on and off by writing FREE CLG (BO 23); with it disabled the outdoor air damper stays at OADPR MINPOS.",
  "setup": [
   "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the factory value is 255.",
   "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6695."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "As shipped, the controller keeps all equipment OFF until it is released to application control (see Siemens start-up procedures).",
   "With a digital room unit (revision 26 and later), a command sent through the room unit puts the matching BACnet input Out Of Service.",
   "Loop gains, biases, output span/start settings and setup codes are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely.",
   "A low temperature detection thermostat on BI 26 is strongly recommended for hot water and steam coils."
  ]
 },
